{
  "id": "016",
  "title": "Nine Months Contract",
  "subtitle": "\"He needed a wife for his custody hearing. I needed ninety thousand dollars for my sister's chemotherapy. We signed.\"",
  "penName": "Harper Lane",
  "genre": "contractMarriage",
  "hook": "My sister was twenty years old and had stage three ovarian cancer and thirty percent insurance coverage. The oncologist said ninety thousand dollars out of pocket. I had three thousand in savings and a job waiting tables. The man at the bar said he would pay me ninety thousand dollars plus a salary for nine months. He needed a wife. He had a fourteen-year-old daughter, a dead ex-wife, and a custody battle with the ex-wife's mother who was trying to take the girl to Connecticut. We had one drink. I signed the contract in his lawyer's office the next morning.",
